Revision history for RPi-RTC-DS3231

0.04 UNREL
    - Added TECHNICAL INFORMATION POD (DEVICE SPECIFICS, REGISTER MAP, ON THE
      WIRE, DATASHEET): chip capabilities, Pi wiring, the 0x00-0x12 register
      map, and the exact I2C frames the XS layer produces, verified against
      the DS3231 datasheet (19-5170 Rev 10)
    - Fixed pre-existing POD nits: hour()'s unresolved clock_hours link, and
      an empty METHODS head1 that podchecker warned on
    - Fixed more POD typos: SYNOPSIS called $rt->sec (should be $rtc->sec),
      temp() misspelled Celsius and Fahrenheit, and the "Auxillary date/time
      methods" heading (plus the matching code comment) misspelled Auxiliary
    - Bundled the datasheet as docs/datasheet/DS3231.pdf and repointed the
      DATASHEET POD section at it instead of the Adafruit-hosted URL
    - Renamed the misspelled $celcius local in temp() to $celsius (cosmetic;
      no API or behaviour change)
    - Removed a stale .claude/settings.local.json entry from MANIFEST (the
      file is untracked and not part of the distribution)
    - Made composed time reads/writes atomic on the bus (XS): hms(),
      date_time() and dt_hash() now take a single coherent burst-read of
      registers 0x00-0x06 (the chip snapshots them into secondary buffers on
      START) instead of stitching several per-register reads a tick could
      tear; date_time('...') now sets the clock with one burst write, seconds
      first (the seconds write resets the countdown chain and the datasheet
      requires the remaining registers within 1s). Added _read_time_burst /
      _write_time_burst XS helpers; day-of-week, 12/24 mode and century bits
      are preserved, and the chip-mutating clock_hours() toggle previously
      used to read the 24-hour value is gone. ON THE WIRE POD updated.
    - Corrected the DS1307 compatibility claim in DESCRIPTION. Verified
      against the DS1307 datasheet: basic timekeeping carries over (same 0x68
      address, 0x00-0x06 BCD register map, 12/24 + AM/PM hour layout), but
      documented three real differences - temp() is invalid (0x11-0x12 are NV
      RAM on a DS1307, which has no temperature sensor); the seconds bit-7 CH
      (clock-halt) bit is masked on read and cleared on write, so a halted
      DS1307 clock is hidden and silently restarted; and the burst reads are
      not snapshot-atomic on a DS1307 (it lacks the DS3231's secondary buffer)
    - Added a Makefile.PL build guard: the family-canonical
      RPi::Const::BuildCheck::i2c_build_check() (via CONFIGURE_REQUIRES), so a
      missing I2C development header now exits NA rather than FAIL on CPAN
      testers; this XS dist previously had no such guard
    - Added t/75-validation.t: HW-free coverage of _write_time()'s field-range
      croaks (year/month/mday/hour/min/sec, all validated before the fd is
      touched, so a bare-blessed object exercises them with no chip), the
      date_time() format croak, and the am_pm()/clock_hours() bad-argument
      croaks; plus temp()/temp('f') sign, two-decimal format and Fahrenheit
      conversion over known Celsius values including the negative path (getTemp
      stubbed) - the room-temperature-gated t/50-temp.t cannot reach sub-zero

0.03    2026-06-22
    - Fixed temp() to normalize its return value to two decimal places in both
      scales; the Fahrenheit conversion could yield a single decimal (e.g.
      71.6) and a 0.25-deg Celsius reading (e.g. 22.5) had the same issue

0.02    2026-06-22
        - Fixed setMonth() to store the month in BCD (was raw binary); months
          10, 11 and 12 were written as illegal BCD (0x0A-0x0C) and corrupted
          the calendar/rollover on the chip
        - Fixed setHour() 12-hour mode to store the hour in BCD (same raw-binary
          bug as setMonth())
        - Fixed getTemp() to sign-extend the temperature MSB so sub-zero
          temperatures decode correctly
        - Routed all BCD time/date register I/O through new setBcdField() /
          getBcdField() helpers, with masks per the DS3231 datasheet, so the
          raw-vs-BCD encoding can no longer diverge
        - Added a simple BCD codec sanity check (t/01-bcd-encoding.t) and
          worst-case raw-register guards in t/40-month.t / t/15-hour.t that fail
          on the old raw write and pass on the BCD write; tightened t/50-temp.t
          to assert the DS3231 operating range. The comprehensive, exhaustive
          proof lives in the rpi-wiringpi test platform

0.01 2018-05-28
        - initial release

